 "notes": "ME-2: LePage led 49.894% to Dunlap 48.307% on first choices (unofficial, all towns), short of 50%, so the state was required to run ranked-choice tabulation starting Nov 9; Dunlap conceded Nov 5. I found no report of the final tabulation or a recount request, so 'called' rests on the concession plus the unofficial count, not a certified result. CT-1 Bronin: 'former Hartford mayor' and Larson's Aug 11 primary loss come from search-result summaries of Connecticut Public/WFSB; the opened page confirms Bronin won and Larson is outgoing. MA: Boston 25 says Democrats won all nine seats and names each winner, but does not give district numbers for McGovern, Clark and Pressley (it says they ran unopposed); their district numbers are taken from the roster (Massachusetts did not redraw for 2026 as far as I saw). NBC Boston reports McGovern and Pressley had no Republican opponent; Clark's November opposition status is unclear but she is reported as a winner. RI-1: one Boston Globe snippet named a different opponent (Kellie Keenan) for Amo than AP-based reports (Allen Waters); does not affect the winner. No certified results checked for any state; all are election-night media/AP calls."
